	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(564.0, -285.0, 369.0, 117.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">A ***workflow*** is made up of **widgets** (*the computational units*) and links (the connection between widgets enabling the *flow of information*): it starts from the top-left hand corner and enrolls left-ro-right and top-to bottom</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/markdown" rect="(-194.0, -580.0, 154.0, 63.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)**</text>
		<arrow id="2" start="(999.0, 285.0)" end="(947.0, 287.0)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<text id="3" type="text/plain" rect="(1007.0, 265.0, 262.0, 57.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">the 3 outgoing flows from the filter do create the 3 different groups</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/markdown" rect="(550.0, 404.0, 82.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**PLOTS**</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/plain" rect="(448.0, 289.0, 92.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">univariate outliers</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/plain" rect="(492.0, 484.0, 111.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">multivariate outliers</text>
		<text id="7" type="text/plain" rect="(-81.0, -237.0, 141.0, 117.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Correlation is an index between 2 numeric variables.</text>
		<text id="8" type="text/markdown" rect="(-80.0, -261.0, 142.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**CORRELATION**</text>
		<text id="9" type="text/markdown" rect="(465.0, -70.0, 112.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**STATISTICS**</text>
		<text id="10" type="text/markdown" rect="(593.0, 221.0, 109.0, 36.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**FILTERS**</text>
		<text id="11" type="text/markdown" rect="(381.0, 78.0, 103.0, 42.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**SAMPLING**</text>
		<text id="12" type="text/markdown" rect="(58.0, 402.0, 92.0, 75.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**MISSING VALUES**</text>
		<text id="13" type="text/markdown" rect="(-76.0, 228.0, 293.0, 142.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">MVs can:
- distort statistics (like mean or correlation), especially if they are a lot
- affect predictive models</text>
		<arrow id="14" start="(164.0, 812.0)" end="(284.0, 831.0)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<text id="15" type="text/markdown" rect="(-80.0, 785.0, 318.0, 255.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**3 strategies** to deal with MVs:
- ***removing*** all rows with at least one MV (loss of data??) - by this widegt
- ***imputing*** average/most frequent label for **that column** - by this widget
- ***predicting*** the value - by a predictive model</text>
		<text id="16" type="text/markdown" rect="(211.0, 523.0, 198.0, 75.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">&lt;u&gt;MVs'&lt;br&gt;
visualization&lt;/u&gt;</text>
		<text id="17" type="text/markdown" rect="(323.0, 733.0, 134.0, 34.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">&lt;u&gt;MVs'&lt;br&gt;management</text>
	</annotations>
